  "description": "QESCEZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H126 Cd2 Ce4 I2 O18. From the CIF bond table, Ce2 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce1 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Cd1 (Cd) has 4 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Cd2 (Cd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.476-3.584 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.21-100.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C54H126Cd2Ce4I2O18.",
